<div class="container mt-4">
  <h1 class="mb-4">About This Application</h1>

  <h3 class="mt-4">Data Sources</h3>
  <p>This Ruby on Rails application uses data collected from two separate data sources:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Dog CEO API:</strong> Used to fetch real dog breed names and dynamic image URLs from public endpoints.</li>
    <li><strong>Faker Gem:</strong> Used to generate animal rescue shelter profiles (names, locations, and contact emails) and supplementary dataset entries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="mt-4">Database Structure & Relationship</h3>
  <p>The application is built around a one-to-many relationship between <strong>Shelter</strong> and <strong>Breed</strong> models:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A <strong>Shelter</strong> has many <strong>Breeds</strong>.</li>
    <li>A <strong>Breed</strong> belongs to a <strong>Shelter</strong> via a foreign key (shelter_id).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The database seeds generate over 200 total records to satisfy project data requirements.</p>

  <div class="mt-4">
    <%= link_to '← Back to Home', root_path, class: 'btn btn-outline-secondary' %>
  </div>
</div>